{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1495405-garou-and-techno-mages-plot-hook-issues","id":1495405,"title":"Garou and techno-mages, plot hook issues.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-10-22T02:03:00-07:00","id":1495405,"title":"Garou and techno-mages, plot hook issues.","content":"Ok, so ........ hear me out. I am assiting with an &quot;open ended&quot; campaign based off of a merger of WTA and MTAs. Players will able to vote and choose a good or evil campaign.<br /> <br /> The Good route is supposedly a tribe of glasswalkers trying to team up with techno mages of the 9 traditions.<br /> <br /> The bad route is Pentex, ie Endron Atomics division employees supported by technocrats of the syndicate. <br /> <br /> What i ask is potential context for these relationships. I need plot hooks to justify inter game interaction.<br /> <br /> I understand garou and mages are largely offput by each other, moreso for tech mages. <br /> -what would modivate a tribe of garou to cooperate with mages?<br /> -what kind of rapport would mages and garou have as allies?<br /> -would the glasswalker be more inclined to cooperate with technomages. If so, how would this manifest?<br /> -what obstacles of trust would need to be crossed from the two to cooperate?<br /> -inversely what would motivate mages to work with garou, and what would their views on their &quot;allies&quot; be.<br /> <br /> The game is meant to be a 2 parter:<br /> 1. The group comes togetther and overcomes an issue that allows the mages and garou to meet and team up.<br /> 2. The coalition of mages and garou take the fight to Pentex.<br /> <br /> The group of players is quite large, garou played by newer players, mages played by older players to assist the Storyteller with magic BS in case players get out of hand. Overall quite experimental.<br /> <br /> Any assistance for inspiration and ideas for this would be much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27527-devilturnip","name":"Devilturnip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T02:48:34-07:00","id":1495410,"title":"","content":"I admit I'm not an expert of MtA, but one hurdle the Tradition mages would run into with the Glass Walkers is that GW technology is as animistic as the rougher tools of other garou. So keep in mind that they would first and foremost rely on the spirit of a machine and its spiritual resonance.<br /> <br /> Another is simply that neither side would really want to reveal too much about themselves. So cyberfetishes and mage creations would be carefully hidden.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T04:07:21-07:00","id":1495415,"title":"","content":"The weird thing here is that technomages tend to be about taking technology and then building it up to the extreme and making it do the impossible through technological means. Glass Walkers do have special tech, but they make it through a marriage of craftsmanship, spirit binding and coopting the tools of the Weaver into their own. The only Tradition that would actually understand them are some very weird Dreamspeakers or members of House Thig. Etherites and VA's would be really, really confused by them.<br /> <br /> An additional complication to very different philosophies is the fact that Mages tend to be seen as bad by the Garou for religious reasons - their powers are abhorrent and literally break down reality and take away the ability of Naming that should not be theirs. That whole thing is compounded by the fact that Caerns are really convenient Nodes that Mages will want to use and/or convert from their sacred nature into something base that just gives them &quot;Their&quot; kind of Quintessence. This means that even the nicest werewolves with the most patience for Mages will be in trouble if others hear what they are up to.<br /> <br /> Now putting both those things aside - the best way to have them cooperate and figure out they are friends is to give them common interests and common enemies. Maybe they all hang out on the Digital Web together, maybe they're part of the same hacktivist coop, maybe they have a familial bond or maybe they are both being assaulted by an enemy they don't understand. A good option would be the Weaver based Men In Black, the strange Drones that are sent to &quot;fix&quot; what the Weaver sees as off, and I'm quite sure Mages or Werewolves would count. Another idea might be that for some reason members and/or family of either side are affected by the OneSong, and the only way they might cure it is to work together, building bonds and friendships.<br /> <br /> As much as I dislike your bad route concept, it's much easier to put into motion. The Wyrm's minions have as many reasons to hate each other as they have to wotrk together, and I could see a powerful Nehandus or BSD Theurge organising a &quot;co-op&quot; project between factions like these for any number of nefarious purposes. They will probably hate each other and backstab each other wherever they can, but at the end of the day, the overlord and the Wyrm's urgings will keep them on task. I pretty much see their power dynamics as Cobra's, just with more actual murder, mayhem and world domination.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T10:05:44-07:00","id":1495437,"title":"","content":"If you want these two groups to work together, they need a common enemy to fight. They also need to be on their own and not be able to rely on more traditional allies (NPCs of their faction).<br /> <br /> So I'd make the Garou PCs members of a small, local rank 1 sept that may only have a few NPCs who handle all the sept duties. I'd make the Technomancer PCs the only members of a local chantry that has just opened up with maybe 1 NPC or so to handle all the things the PCs won't be doing. With no one else able to help them, they need to work with each other. Maybe even make it clear that the sept and chantry here are so minor or disreputable, that nobody will ever bother to help them. Maybe it is even a place they send the screw ups, misfits, and characters who offended the powerful and are being punished for it.<br /> <br /> The most obvious antagonist that could unite them is PENTEX. Pick one of the subsidiaries (or create your own) that makes sense for whatever city you place the game in, something that could be massively important in that city. Create separate projects that threaten the caern and chantry separately, and then projects that would be seen as threats by both.<br /> <br /> You may also want to give them something in common as well, although they may not know it yet. Perhaps there is a small fictional company both Glasswalker and Technocracy PCs have a common ownership or influence in. Or that their separate companies are located in the same business park or skyrise building. Or even something so minor like they both like the same neighborhood coffee shop. It could be allies or mentors that they have in common through Backgrounds. While you should have some ideas of your own that pitch, or work into the backgrounds of the PCs, I would recommend you ask your players to collaborate together to come up with ideas that resonate with them.<br /> <br /> You might also want to make a Kinfolk an important kinfolk for the Garou, but who is also valuable to the Technomancers. Perhaps even make this person beloved by all the PCs, and then start the chronicle by showing he is dead (actually murdered by PENTEX). That brings the two sides together to investigate the suspicious nature of his death. Maybe even ask each PC to invent the reason why they loved this NPC so much that they would want vengeance/justice over the people who killed him.<br /> <br /> I always think the burden should be on the players to come up with reasons for their PCs to work together as part of their character creation, especially when they are playing rival groups that normally do not work together. The ST should have ideas of her own she will pitch, but her main job is to facilitate the players and help them understand what ideas will work in your chronicle, and which ideas won't fit.<br /> <br /> I think a good potential end plot would be to host the bad guys in the Umbral realm of Cybertown (known as Dystopia by Mages). That will allow you to do over-the-top cinematic city assault scenes that can't be done in the real world, but would look great in that Umbral realm.<br /> <br /> That would be my pitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 10-23-2022, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-22T10:55:11-07:00","id":1495442,"title":"","content":"Elephant in the thread - you might find that you have to make a hard call during the game about what setup of metaphysics is factually correct, because Garou and mages can't both be correct. Their respective games are exclusive about that and will not play nice if &quot;higher order&quot; questions come up.<br /> <br /> An alternate antagonist that could unite the group is Shinzui, essentially the Weaver's answer to Pentex, which is 1) more unified, 2) doesn't play around like Pentex (in the end scenario book, they tear it to pieces in weeks at the behest of the greater Weaver-spirits that can practically use them like puppets), and 3) ultimately was created by Garou and kin in an attempt to use corporate power structures against big corporations, and it all went horribly and terribly right. You can read up on them in Book of the Weaver and Apocalypse. Technomancers might look askance at what might otherwise be an ally when their Drones take exception to technomancers still spelling magic with the Special K (read: still practicing reality-warping sphere effects that the Weaver doesn't like) and start walking all over the Technocracy's HIT Marks and other constructs (Drones can actually regenerate even better than the Garou, like Sid 6.7 in Virtuosity - they even recover from agg as if it were mere lethal damage) and giving the Technocracy a taste of the pogrom that it inflicted on other mages.<br /> <br /> Just be careful not to kill the mages by accident. Combat Drones are, much like front-line combat fomori, meant to hold up against Crinos werewolves, so you might need to have them suddenly pull away on other business to keep some PCs alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}